---
import "../../../../packages/ui/src/brand/brand.css";
import "../../../../packages/ui/src/glass/glass.css";
import "../installer.css";

import Footer from "../../../../packages/ui/src/brand/Footer.astro";
import Header from "../../../../packages/ui/src/brand/Header.astro";
import ThemeInit from '../../../../packages/ui/src/brand/ThemeInit.astro';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head><ThemeInit external />
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Host the installer yourself · SAM</title>
    <link rel="icon" href="/sam-head.png" />
    
    
    
    <script is:inline src="/guide.js" defer></script>
  </head>
  <body class="sam-form">
    <Header compact icon="/brand-icon.png" />
    <main class="privacy-main">

      <span class="badge">Same source. Your host.</span>
      <h1>Run the installer<br /><span class="gradient-text">on your terms.</span></h1>
      <p class="intro">
        Prefer to handle Cloudflare access yourself? Deploy this same open-source installer in your
        own account.
      </p>
<p>No GitHub account is needed to get SAM running in Cloudflare. Signing in afterwards requires GitHub, GitLab or Google; there is no email login.</p>
      <div class="privacy-content sam-glass sam-glass-rim">
        <h2>1. Get the source</h2>
        <p>
          You’ll need Node.js 22+, pnpm 9.15.9, a Workers Paid account, and an active domain in
          Cloudflare.
          <a id="source" href="https://github.com/raphaeltm/simple-agent-manager"
            >Inspect the deployed source →</a
          >
        </p>
        <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/raphaeltm/simple-agent-manager.git
cd simple-agent-manager
<span id="revision-command"># For an unmerged preview, check out the revision linked above.
</span>pnpm install --frozen-lockfile</code></pre>
        <h2>2. Configure your deployment</h2>
        <p>
          Set <code>CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN</code> and <code>CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID</code> through your
          shell’s secret manager. Never commit credentials or paste them into chat.
        </p>
        <p>
          The deployment token needs Account Settings Read, Workers Scripts Edit, OAuth Client
          Read/Write, and zone permissions for Workers Custom Domains and Workers Routes. Scope it
          to the account and zone you intend to use.
        </p>
        <pre><code>export BASE_DOMAIN=example.com
pnpm --filter @simple-agent-manager/installer run deploy</code></pre>
        <h2>3. Open your installer</h2>
        <p>
          The script deploys at <code>https://install.example.com</code>, registers a private OAuth
          client, and saves its credentials as Worker secrets. Keep those credentials private.
          Rerunning preserves the existing client and secret.
        </p>
        <p>
          While this prototype is unmerged, check out the revision shown by “Inspect the deployed
          source” before deploying. The default branch may not include the installer yet.
        </p>
        <h2>Before sharing it with others</h2>
        <p>
          Private OAuth clients work for members of their parent account. Serving other users
          requires Cloudflare’s
          <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/fundamentals/oauth/create-an-oauth-client/"
            >publisher verification and public promotion</a
          >. Promotion is permanent and is never performed automatically by this script.
        </p>
        <h2>What you’re deploying</h2>
        <p>
          The standard command deploys bootstrap-only mode, separate from SAM. This preview branch
          adds durable owner recovery: save the browser-generated credential before claiming your
          service. The hosted address may still run an earlier revision; check its source version.
        </p>
        <p>
          Experimental full installation and update machinery is under development. It is not
          enabled by this command and has not completed authenticated OAuth, credential-revocation,
          and full in-account build validation. Use the established SAM self-hosting guide for a
          complete installation. No working full-mode enablement recipe is provided yet.
        </p>
        <p><a href="/privacy.html">Review permissions & privacy →</a></p>
      </div>
    </main>
    <Footer compact icon="/sam-head.png"><a href="/privacy.html">Permissions & privacy</a><a href="/self-host.html">Self-host</a><span id="version"></span></Footer>
  </body>
</html>
